@100  = ~Jarnip in ToB: A New Merchant in Saradush~
@101  = ~Must be installed on BG2, BGT, BG2EE or EET~
@102  = ~Jarnip~
@103  = ~Jarnip's Wares~
@104  = ~Bane of the Innocent +4~
@105  = ~The first victims of this sword were not warriors. They were pilgrims. Peasants. Beggars. Those who could not fight back.

Long ago, this forsaken blade belonged to an unnamed holy champion who was suddenly stripped of his deity's grace. Instead of seeking penance, he chose the path of vengeance. It is said that the slaughter of the followers of his former faith was so great that the screams of his victims became permanently imbued within the blade.

Bane of the Innocent strikes terror into the hearts of those who face it and does not tolerate the touch of the righteous. Because of unspeakable atrocities committed with it in the past, only those who follow the path of the antipaladin, or who have become fallen paladins, can wield it.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
- Fire Resistance: +20%
- Characters of Good or Neutral alignment are slain upon equipping this sword

Combat abilities:
- Touch of Terror: 25% chance on hit to cause the target to panic for 4 rounds
- Dooming Presence: 5% chance on hit that all enemies within a 15-ft. radius panic and receive a -2 penalty to Armor Class, hit rolls, and damage rolls for 1 turn

THAC0: +4 
Damage: 2d4+4 (slashing), +2d4 (fire)
Speed Factor: 4 
Proficiency Type: Bastard Sword
Type: One-handed
Requires:
 10 Strength

Weight: 3~
@106  = ~The Triumphant +5~
@107  = ~According to legend, The Triumphant first belonged to a barbarian king of Narfell who perished while defending his homeland from an invading horde of demons from the Endless Wastes. The sword was said to have been found on the battlefield after its wielder had single-handedly defeated an entire army. No body was ever found. Only the sword remained, lying amid the dead.

Since that time, The Triumphant has appeared in countless sagas of the northern barbarian tribes, becoming a powerful symbol of might and perseverance. Some say that whoever claims the sword is destined for greatness, while others believe that the blade simply finds those who are worthy of it.

Whatever the truth, those who take up The Triumphant soon discover that even impossible odds can be overcome.

STATISTICS:

Equipped Abilities:
- Strength: +2

Combat Abilities:
- Heroic Inspiration: While enraged, increases Armor Class by 2, Critical Strike chance by 5%, and grants an extra attack per round
- Furious Strikes: Critical hits knock the target back and deal an additional 2d12 slashing damage

THAC0: +5
Damage: 1d10+5 (slashing)
Speed Factor: 5
Proficiency Type: Two-handed Sword
Type: Two-handed
Requires:
 16 Strength

Weight: 15~
@108  = ~Neverwinter Sapphire +3~
@109  = ~This richly adorned off-hand dagger bears the crest of the city of Neverwinter and has a teardrop-shaped sapphire set into its pommel. The dagger is enchanted to deflect enemy blows, and its sapphire has the power to summon illusory copies of the wielder. Because its enchantment requires a basic understanding of magic, only thieves and bards can use it.

STATISTICS:

Equipped Abilities:
- Armor Class: +2
- Attacks per round: +1

Combat Abilities:
- Sapphire Guard: On a critical miss, casts Mirror Image on the wielder

THAC0: +3
Damage: 1d4+3 (piercing)
Speed Factor: 0
Proficiency Type: Dagger
Type: One-handed
Requires:
 3 Strength

Weight: 1~
@110  = ~Vigilant Eye +4~
@111  = ~Holy Shield of Protection: Vigilant Eye

This intricately decorated shield is forged from polished azure steel and bears the holy symbol of Helm. The blessing granted to it by the Vigilant One is truly incredible, as it extends beyond its bearer and protects all allies who stand beside the paladin.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
- Armor Class: +5
- Saving Throws: +1
- Magic Resistance: +10%
- Aura of Protection: All party members gain:
   +1 bonus to Armor Class
   +1 bonus to all saving throws

Requires:
 13 Strength
 13 Wisdom

Weight: 8~
@112  = ~Axe of the Worldbreaker +4~
@113  = ~This mighty adamantine two-handed axe belonged to Blaiz the Worldbreaker, a giant warlord who once established a kingdom in the Spine of the World. After gathering an army of ogres, trolls, and orcs, Blaiz marched south, leaving a trail of destruction in his wake. His reign of terror finally ended when a band of adventurers from Luskan slew him in battle and claimed the axe as their prize.

STATISTICS:

Equipped Abilities:
- Immunity to Fear
- Regenerate 1 Hit Point every 2 seconds

Combat Abilities:
- Relentless Onslaught: Each hit deals an additional 4 points of slashing damage and heals the wielder for 4 Hit Points. This will not heal beyond the wielder's maximum
- The World Crumbles: Critical hits deal an additional 10 points of slashing damage and heal the wielder for 10 Hit Points. The target must Save vs. Death at -2 or be stunned for 1 round

THAC0: +4
Damage: 1d10+4 (slashing)
Speed Factor: 5
Proficiency Type: Axe
Type: Two-handed
Requires:
 17 Strength

Weight: 25~
@114  = ~Light of Eldath +5~
@115  = ~This unique greater Staff of the Woodlands was a personal gift from Eldath to the High Vychlaran of Rashemen. Blessed by the Green Goddess herself, the staff embodies her peaceful domain, granting an incredible blessing and calling upon the judgment of nature against anyone who dares to harm its wielder.

STATISTICS:

Equipped Abilities:
- Fire and Cold Resistance: +20%
- Armor Class: +2
- Saving Throws: +1
- Wisdom: +2

Combat Abilities:
- Emerald Rebuke: Any creature that strikes the wielder in melee must save vs. Wand at -2 or suffer 1d6+5 poison damage and become entangled for 4 rounds

THAC0: +5
Damage: 1d6+5 (crushing)
Speed Factor: 0
Proficiency Type: Quarterstaff
Type: Two-handed
Requires:
 10 Dexterity
 15 Wisdom

Weight: 4~
@116  = ~Helm of the Broken Weave~
@117  = ~Forged by dwarven smiths during an ancient war against the archmages of Netheril, this heavy helm is laced with veins of black meteoric iron that seem to drink in magical energy. Wizards standing nearby often describe an oppressive sensation, as though the Weave itself grows thin in its presence.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
- Armor Class: +1
- Magic Damage Resistance: +30%
- Protects against critical hits

Combat abilities:
- Anti-Magic Aura: Enemy arcane spellcasters within 30 ft. cast spells at +2 casting time and suffer 25% spell failure (Wizard Slayer only)

Weight: 2~
@118  = ~Cloak of the Crimson Abbot~
@119  = ~Long ago, this legendary cloak was a hereditary artifact worn by the abbots of the Monastery of the Crimson Rose in Shou Lung. After the monastery was raided and destroyed by the Tuigan Horde, the artifact was thought lost forever. How it eventually found its way to the Sword Coast remains unknown, but there is little doubt that it is one of the most powerful monk relics in the Realms.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
- Hit Points: +10
- Attacks per round: +1 (Monk only)

Combat abilities:
- Scarlet Palm: Each successful melee hit with fists has a 33% chance to stun the target for 1 round (save vs. Spell negates)

Weight: 4~
@120  = ~Robe of Balagos~
@121  = ~This robe was crafted by the legendary red dragon Balagos for when he assumed human form. Later, he gifted it to his human worshippers. Woven from heavy Calimshan silk and adorned with the scales of the great wyrm, the robe contains a fragment of Balagos's own draconic power. However, only those touched by dragon blood can unlock its full potential.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
- Armor Class: 4
- Decrease casting time by 2
- Physical Damage resistance: +30% (Red Dragon Disciple only)
- Fire damage dealt by the wearer: +20% (Red Dragon Disciple only)

Charge abilities:
- Casts Dragon Breath once per day
 Damage: 20d10 (Save vs. Breath for half)
 Area: 15-ft. radius
 Does not harm party members

Weight: 3~
@122  = ~Torm's Gauntlets~
@123  = ~These gauntlets are said to have been worn by Torm himself during the Time of Troubles. Whether the legend is true or not, they grant the wearer a powerful blessing, strengthening their resolve and improving their divine spellcasting skills.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
- Armor Class: +1
- Saving Throws: +1
- Spell Casting Speed Improved by 2 (Clerics and Paladins only)
- Divine Casting Level: +1 (Clerics and Paladins only)

Weight: 1~
@124  = ~Herbert's Coat of Fortune +5~
@125  = ~
This exceptional leather coat once belonged to Herbert Schwarz, a famous Waterdhavian duelist whose adventures along the Sword Coast became the subject of innumerable folk tales. Herbert was known for being able to escape from even the most dangerous situations, a talent many attributed to his enchanted armor. Durable, lightweight, and enchanted with a permanent blessing of fortune, this armor is the dream of any adventurer.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
- Luck: +1 (Swashbuckler only)

Combat abilities:
- Avoid Death: When the wielder's Hit Points fall below 25%, grants 20 temporary hit points, +5 to saves vs. Death, and immunity to death magic for 1 round. This effect can only occur once every 1 turn

Armor Class: 2 (0 vs. slashing, 1 vs. piercing and missile), 1 (Swashbuckler)
Requires:
 8 Strength

Weight: 10~
